+## D12 — Bounded five-demo ambiguity (review-218682899634147d)
+
+On unchanged source `bc804b9fdda08451fbd63dbfb2918d0f1e1e84074d71db7cf97973555722fe2b`,
+the ordinary seed-0, medium-difficulty lesson at samples 0–4 teaches identity,
+CW, 180, CCW and LR; sample 5 is the first UD query. An executable rival that
+uses the inferred transform except falling back to CW for UD fits all five
+demonstrations and disagrees on query 5. The current `lesson_identifiable` gate
+returns no findings because its finite rival set tests a combined identity/UD
+fallback, which the identity demonstration rejects, but omits this UD-only rival.
+
+The retained `checks/4c17a205be08/peer-report.json` contains the original lesson,
+canonical and rival programs, all outputs, and source/runtime identities;
+`peer_probe.py` replays it. All 36 evaluations (canonical plus three rivals on
+five demos/four queries) used protected Racket through the native `wrap_rule`
+pipeline. Canonical labels agreed with the mirror. This is a finite teaching
+gap, not a label defect or a claim of universal unlearnability. Production and
+canonical sources remain unchanged. The next concrete repair is to add
+single-missing-transform rivals and require coverage of all six branches,
+preferably by using six demonstrations for this six-branch schedule. Preserve
+the original five-demo lesson for alternative-answer evidence. The native
+candidate is `workspace/parametric/evidence/alternative-solutions/five-demo-ud-fallback.json`;
+its two hypotheses and original lesson are source-bound for owner refresh. Owner review
+and any integration remain pending; no approval or training change is claimed.
